  ],
  "text": "A chilli is spicy specifically so that mammals will leave it alone. A plant cannot move. So the seed has to travel without it. Some seeds fly. A wing on a seed is just a slower way to land. Some hitch a ride. Hooks that grab any coat that brushes past. Some float. A coconut can cross an ocean and land ready to grow. And some pay for delivery. Sweet fruit in exchange for a lift. Which brings us back to the chilli. Birds cannot taste capsaicin at all. Birds fly much further, and they do not grind seeds up with molars. So the plant built a chemical to filter customers. And we went looking for it. One of these every day. Follow so you do not miss tomorrow.",
  "voice": "802e3bc2b27e49c2995d23ef70e6ac89",
  "model": "s2.1-pro-free"
}
